<title>USA: Calif. Gov. signs law enforcement funding bill.</title>
<headline>Calif. Gov. signs law enforcement funding bill.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>California Gov. Pete Wilson signed legislation on Friday to boost funding for several law enforcement programs in the state.</p>
<p>Senate Bill 350, by Democratic Senator Barbara Lee, appropriates nearly $11.5 million in federal funds for allocation to law enforcement, prosecution, victim services and other programs, Wilson, a Republican, said.</p>
